
SimHash is length-sensitive: the same one-sentence edit, by document size

   words   median    p90    max
--------------------------------
     ~75      6.0     10     10
    ~150      4.0      7     10
    ~325      2.0      6      8
    ~800      2.0      4      5
  a short page needs a far looser threshold than a long one for the same edit

Near-duplicate vs unrelated pairs (450 and 150 pairs, ~325-word documents)

  near-duplicates: median 4 bits, max 16
  unrelated:       median 32 bits, min 24
  the gap between 16 and 24 is why a threshold exists at all

 threshold  near caught  false pos  needs bands
------------------------------------------------
         3       50.0%       0.0%            4
         5       67.1%       0.0%            6
         7       80.0%       0.0%            8  <- default
         9       87.8%       0.0%           10
        12       97.3%       0.0%           13
        16      100.0%       0.0%           17
        20      100.0%       0.0%           21

  bands must exceed the threshold for the pigeonhole guarantee and must
  divide 64, so 7 (8 bands of 8 bits) is the most sensitive setting that
  keeps both the guarantee and selective bucket keys.

Bloom filter against a plain set

      urls     bloom   set (est)   bytes/url    error
----------------------------------------------------
    10,000     0.01M        1.0M        1.20    0.90%
   100,000     0.12M       10.0M        1.20        -
 1,000,000     1.20M      100.0M        1.20        -

  ~80x smaller, at a 1% chance of skipping a page that was never crawled.
  Worth it at a hundred million URLs; not at ten thousand, which is why
  the exact set is the default.

